Transcripts — third-party components
====================================

Portions of the macOS application derive from Scribe
(https://github.com/BlueAcornInc/scribe), by Blue Acorn iCi.

Scribe continues as its own project. When it is published under the MIT
licence, that licence's attribution clause applies to this derivation and its
copyright notice belongs here verbatim — MIT permits building proprietary works
from it, on condition the notice travels along.

The iOS app has no third-party dependencies. The list below applies to the
macOS build only.

FluidAudio — https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio
    Apache License 2.0. Speaker diarization — the "who said what" pass over the
    other side of a call.

Speaker diarization models (downloaded at first use, macOS only)
    FluidInference/speaker-diarization-coreml — CC BY 4.0
    https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/speaker-diarization-coreml

    Derived from pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1, also CC BY 4.0
    https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1

    Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    CC BY 4.0 permits commercial use and redistribution, including in a
    proprietary application, on condition of attribution — which is what this
    entry is. The models are converted to Core ML by FluidInference; they are
    used here unmodified.

mlx-swift, mlx-swift-examples — https://github.com/ml-explore
    MIT. In-process LLM inference for the summarization tier.

swift-transformers, swift-jinja — https://github.com/huggingface
    Apache License 2.0. Requires this NOTICE to be preserved.

swift-collections, swift-numerics — https://github.com/apple
    Apache License 2.0.

GzipSwift — https://github.com/1024jp/GzipSwift
    zlib/BSD.

Models downloaded at runtime (macOS only) carry their own terms; a model is not
covered by the licence of the library that loads it.
